"My mother made me a suit: erect ears, a fluffy tail on his pants, even white gloves were found. A poem about a bunny read, I jump out 
and let's jump around the Christmas tree... In the hall, a standing ovation, full of delight, laughter, I am also delighted with my success. I jumped one lap, went to the second, the applause does not stop, I get excited for the third... But then, for some reason, the teacher comes on stage and says something, dragging me backstage. It turns out that I put on bunny pants backwards...".

